Read the SQLite database location from DATABASE_URL.

Why: upstream/server/prisma/schema.prisma hard-codes file:../storage/anythingllm.db, relative to
the schema, so the database always lands inside the server code directory. In the packaged app
that directory is inside the signed, read-only bundle. With env("DATABASE_URL") the AskFiles
process manager points both prisma migrate deploy and the server at
file:<dataDir>/storage/anythingllm.db. Run prisma generate after applying this patch.
Without DATABASE_URL, Prisma fails with: Environment variable not found: DATABASE_URL.

Paths are relative to upstream/. Apply from the repository root with
  git apply --directory=upstream patches/002-database-url.patch

diff --git a/server/prisma/schema.prisma b/server/prisma/schema.prisma
index 65cfd6c..0fd7a59 100644
--- a/server/prisma/schema.prisma
+++ b/server/prisma/schema.prisma
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ generator client {
 // }
 datasource db {
   provider = "sqlite"
-  url      = "file:../storage/anythingllm.db"
+  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
 }
 
 model api_keys {
